---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Code from '@/components/site/Code.astro';
import { href } from '@/lib/site';
import { CodeTabs } from '@/components/animate-ui/components/animate/code-tabs';
import RbacFaq from '@/components/site/RbacFaq';

const toc = [
  ['prereqs', 'Prerequisites'],
  ['install', '1. Install logcloak'],
  ['optin', '2. Opt in a namespace'],
  ['choosing', 'Choosing your approach'],
  ['policy', '3. MaskingPolicy (platform team)'],
  ['annotations', '4. Pod annotations (developer)'],
  ['verify', '5. Verify raw logs are clean'],
  ['reject', '6. Reject invalid regex at admission'],
  ['scan', 'Audit logs before you deploy'],
  ['mesh', '7. Service mesh compatibility'],
  ['logs-ref', 'kubectl logs behaviour'],
  ['uninstall', 'Uninstall'],
];
---
<Layout title="Guide — logcloak" description="A complete walkthrough of installing and configuring logcloak, from scratch to verified masked output." current="/guide">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-1 gap-10 px-6 py-14 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_200px]">
    <article class="prose-doc min-w-0">
      <p class="mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Hands-on guide</p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Install logcloak, verify masked output</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">
        A complete walkthrough — from a bare cluster to verified masked logs. Every command and output
        below is real, captured from a live k3s/k3d cluster.
      </p>

      <h2 id="prereqs">Prerequisites</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Kubernetes 1.24+ (k3s, GKE, EKS, or AKS)</li>
        <li>Helm 3.x</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="install">1. Install logcloak</h2>
      <p>Add the repo and install the chart into its own namespace:</p>
      <Code code={`helm repo add logcloak https://1mr0-tech.github.io/logcloak\nhelm repo update\nhelm install logcloak logcloak/logcloak \\\n  --namespace logcloak --create-namespace`} />
      <p>Verify both containers (webhook + controller) are running in each pod:</p>
      <Code code={`kubectl get pods -n logcloak\n# NAME                        READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\n# logcloak-68c64b8fb4-67gmb   2/2     Running   0          50s\n# logcloak-68c64b8fb4-bj6gp   2/2     Running   0          50s`} />
      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">TLS needs no configuration.</strong> logcloak generates a
        self-signed certificate on first startup, stores it in a Secret, and patches its own
        <code>MutatingWebhookConfiguration</code> with the CA. The cert is valid for one year and
        rotates automatically before expiry — track time-to-expiry with the
        <code>logcloak_tls_cert_expiry_seconds</code> Prometheus gauge.
      </p>
      <p>
        A <code>PodDisruptionBudget</code> (<code>minAvailable: 1</code> by default) ships with the
        chart, and both webhook and controller emit structured JSON logs. Prometheus metrics are on
        port <code>9090</code> — see the <a href={href('/docs')}>docs page</a> for the full metric
        reference.
      </p>

      <h2 id="optin">2. Opt a namespace in</h2>
      <p>logcloak is opt-in. Only labelled namespaces get sidecar injection — this keeps system namespaces untouched.</p>
      <Code code={`kubectl create namespace production\nkubectl label namespace production logcloak.io/inject=true`} />
      <blockquote>Any pod created from this point forward gets the sidecar injected automatically. Existing running pods are unaffected until restarted.</blockquote>

      <h2 id="choosing">Choosing your masking approach</h2>
      <p>logcloak has two ways to define what gets masked. Use them together — annotations extend a policy, they never remove rules from it.</p>
      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-border bg-card">
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"></th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">MaskingPolicy</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">Pod annotation</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-foreground">Who sets it</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">Platform / security team</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">Developer</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-foreground">Scope</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">All matching pods in a namespace</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">One pod only</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-foreground">Can override policy?</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">—</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">No — extends, never removes</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-foreground">Requires cluster access?</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">Yes</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-muted-foreground">No — just deployment YAML</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="policy">3. MaskingPolicy (platform team)</h2>
      <p>A <code>MaskingPolicy</code> defines masking rules for pods matching a selector in a namespace. No selector means every pod in the namespace.</p>
      <Code code={`# masking-policy.yaml\napiVersion: logcloak.io/v1alpha1\nkind: MaskingPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: pii-baseline\n  namespace: production\nspec:\n  patterns:\n    - name: email\n      builtin: email\n    - name: phone\n      builtin: phone-e164\n    - name: otp\n      builtin: otp-6digit\n    - name: auth-token\n      regex: 'Bearer\\\\s+[A-Za-z0-9\\\\-._~+/]+=*'\n  redactWith: "[REDACTED]"`} />
      <Code code={`kubectl apply -f masking-policy.yaml\n# maskingpolicy.logcloak.io/pii-baseline created`} />

      <h3>Built-in pattern names</h3>
      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">email</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">RFC 5321 email addresses</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">phone-e164</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">E.164 international phone numbers</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">phone-us</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">US phone number formats</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">otp-6digit</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">Standalone 6-digit numeric codes</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">credit-card</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">13–19 digit card numbers</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">jwt</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">eyJ… JWT tokens</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">ipv4-private</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">RFC 1918 private IP addresses</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">uuid</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">UUID v4</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">iban</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">International Bank Account Numbers</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-primary">ssn</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">US Social Security Numbers (XXX-XX-XXXX)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Targeting specific services with a selector</h3>
      <Code code={`spec:\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app.kubernetes.io/name: payment-service\n  patterns:\n    - name: credit-card\n      builtin: credit-card`} />

      <h2 id="annotations">4. Pod annotations (developer)</h2>
      <p>Developers extend masking with app-specific patterns, without touching the cluster-wide policy.</p>

      <div class="not-prose my-4">
        <CodeTabs
          client:visible
          lang="yaml"
          codes={{
            'built-in pattern': 'annotations:\n  logcloak.io/patterns: "uuid,iban"',
            'custom regex': "annotations:\n  logcloak.io/regex-<name>: '<your-regex>'",
            'JSON field masking': 'annotations:\n  logcloak.io/fields: "password,token,api_key,card_number"',
          }}
        />
      </div>

      <p>Field masking recurses into nested objects and arrays, runs before regex rules, and applies to lines that begin with <code>{'{'}</code>. You can combine all three on one pod:</p>
      <Code code={`annotations:\n  logcloak.io/patterns: "email,jwt"\n  logcloak.io/fields: "password,secret,api_key"\n  logcloak.io/regex-order-id: 'ORD-[0-9]{8}'`} />
      <p>Field masking also works as a cluster-wide <code>MaskingPolicy</code> rule:</p>
      <Code code={`spec:\n  patterns:\n    - name: password-field\n      field: password\n    - name: token-field\n      field: api_token`} />

      <h2 id="verify">5. Verify raw logs are clean</h2>
      <p>Confirm raw PII never reached the node's log files:</p>
      <Code code={`sudo grep -r 'user@shop.com\\|card=4111\\|otp=847291' /var/log/containers/ 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n# 0`} />

      <h2 id="reject">6. Reject invalid regex at admission</h2>
      <p>Custom regex is validated at pod admission time. Unsafe patterns (lookaheads, backreferences) are rejected before the pod ever starts:</p>
      <Code code={`kubectl run bad-pod -n production --image=busybox:1.36 \\\n  --annotations='logcloak.io/regex-bad=(?=lookahead)' -- sh -c 'echo test'\n\n# Error from server: admission webhook "mutate.logcloak.io" denied the request:\n# invalid regex in annotation "logcloak.io/regex-bad": unsafe regex construct "(?=" detected`} />

      <h2 id="scan">Audit logs before you deploy</h2>
      <p><code>logcloak scan</code> checks what PII is currently leaking from any log source — no cluster required. Install the CLI binary from the <a href="https://github.com/1mr0-tech/logcloak/releases">GitHub releases page</a>.</p>
      <Code code={`kubectl logs my-pod | logcloak scan\nlogcloak scan /var/log/app.log`} />
      <Code code={`line 42     user [REDACTED:email] placed order        [email]\n\nlogcloak scan summary\nTotal lines:     1234\nLines with PII:  1 (0.1%)\nPattern hits:\n  email:               1\n\nProtect these logs → kubectl label namespace <ns> logcloak.io/inject=true`} />
      <p>Also available: <code>logcloak validate '&lt;regex&gt;'</code> to check RE2-safety before deploying, and <code>logcloak preview '&lt;regex&gt;' [file]</code> to test masking output without touching a cluster.</p>

      <h2 id="mesh">7. Service mesh compatibility</h2>
      <p>logcloak is safe alongside Istio, Linkerd, and any other mesh — meshes intercept network traffic; logcloak intercepts stdout. These containers are always skipped: <code>istio-proxy</code>, <code>linkerd-proxy</code>, <code>envoy</code>, <code>envoy-sidecar</code>, <code>kuma-sidecar</code>, <code>consul-sidecar</code>, <code>vault-agent</code>, <code>config-reloader</code>.</p>
      <p>For anything else (a postgres sidecar, a monitoring agent), exclude it explicitly:</p>
      <Code code={`metadata:\n  annotations:\n    logcloak.io/exclude-containers: "postgres,redis,datadog-agent"`} />

      <h2 id="logs-ref">kubectl logs behaviour reference</h2>
      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-primary">kubectl logs &lt;pod&gt;</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">Masked output (logcloak is the default container)</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/60"><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-primary">kubectl logs &lt;pod&gt; -c logcloak</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">Same masked output</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-primary">kubectl logs &lt;pod&gt; -c app</td><td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted-foreground">Empty — app stdout is redirected to the FIFO</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="uninstall">Uninstall</h2>
      <Code code={`helm uninstall logcloak -n logcloak\nkubectl delete crd maskingpolicies.logcloak.io\nkubectl delete namespace production`} />
      <p>Helm never deletes CRDs on uninstall — that's Helm's own behaviour, not logcloak's, so the explicit <code>kubectl delete crd</code> step above is required if you want <code>MaskingPolicy</code> resources gone too. Already-injected pods keep running with their sidecar until restarted.</p>

      <div class="not-prose mt-10">
        <RbacFaq client:visible />
      </div>
    </article>

    <aside class="hidden lg:block">
      <div class="sticky top-20 space-y-1 border-l border-border pl-4 text-sm">
        <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">On this page</p>
        {toc.map(([id, label]) => (
          <a href={`#${id}`} class="block py-1 text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary">{label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
